        }
      ],
      "explanation": "RC6 is met: red flags for mediastinal mass/peri-operative waiting were repeatedly taught, including dyspnea/orthopnea, swelling, hemoptysis, chest pain, fever/systemic decline, voice/swallowing changes, and instructions not to wait for routine follow-up.",
      "issue_kind": "none",
